# Media Library

The administrator may:

- Upload media
- Search media
- Reuse existing media
- Select media from the library
- Upload new media
- Delete unused media after confirmation

# Image Processing

When an image is uploaded:

- Accept a large source image from the administrator.
- Validate and decode it on the server.
- Resize oversized dimensions.
- Preserve aspect ratio.
- Remove metadata.
- Convert to WebP where appropriate.
- Compress to a web-optimized quality.
- Store one optimized version only.
- Do not save the oversized original file.

Use `next/image` for public rendering.

Use responsive sizes and lazy loading.

Allow cover-image cropping where required.

# Recipe Media

A recipe may contain:

- One required cover image
- Up to 6 additional images or short media items

The interface must show the current count.

# SEO Defaults

Generate automatically:

- SEO title from the content title
- SEO description from the content description or article text
- Slug from the title
- Open Graph image from the cover image

All automatic values remain editable.

# Technical SEO

Include:

- Semantic heading hierarchy
- Unique metadata
- Canonical URLs
- Open Graph
- Structured data
- Breadcrumbs
- Dynamic sitemap
- robots.txt
- Published and updated dates
- Alt text for meaningful images

Use relevant Schema.org types:

- Organization
- Person
- Article
- Recipe
- BreadcrumbList
- WebSite